  "description": "VENLEF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C33 H49 Gd5 O9,2(C4 H10 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd4 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.392-4.884 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.14-170.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C33H49Gd5O9.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
